<!-- Load shared doc header and nav -->
<%- include('partials/header.ejs') %>
    <%- include('partials/main_nav.ejs') %>

        <!-- projects content with shared portfolio layout -->
        <main class="container">
            <h1>
                <%= title %>
            </h1>

            <section>
                <h2>Hangman Game</h2>
                <p>
                    This project was a culminating assignment for INFR1101.
                    My group and I recreated the popular Hangman game using Python.
                    We included single-player and multiplayer modes for people
                    who wanted to play with friends. We incorporated concepts
                    learned in the course, such as file handling, loops, and functions.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Banking System</h2>
                <p>
                    This project was a culminating assignment for INFR2141.
                    My group and I created a banking system using Python.
                    Individuals could deposit, withdraw, transfer, check balances,
                    and apply for loans. We used inheritance, polymorphism,
                    encapsulation, and abstraction, which we learned throughout
                    the course.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>INFR2411 Case Study</h2>
                <p>
                    My group and I were tasked with connecting a company's three
                    corporate offices to the same network in a mock scenario.
                    We created a simulated environment in Packet Tracer and
                    configured protocols and features learned throughout the
                    semester, including BGP, VLANs, EtherChannels, trunking, and VTP.
                    We also developed a solution for accessing the network remotely
                    while maintaining network integrity.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Napkin Design</h2>
                <p>
                    This BUSI1600 assignment involved creating a rough estimate
                    of the revenue and expenses of a business we would start.
                    Once I began, I realized that even simplifying a business
                    to a napkin design involved many complexities.
                </p>
            </section>
        </main>

        <!-- Load shared footer and nav script. -->
        <%- include('partials/footer.ejs') %>